      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "monarchy_and_national_identity",
      "label": "The British monarchy as a symbol of national identity",
      "description": "The British monarchy, particularly Queen Elizabeth II, is deeply embedded in British national identity and history. She represented continuity, tradition, and the state. The meme’s violent text is a deliberate attack on this symbol, using her status to express anger or hostility. This requires background knowledge of the monarchy’s role in British society to understand the meme’s provocative nature.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
